#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0437 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: On a given record, AVALCATy is populated and AVALCAyN is not populated
#note "avalcat1 populated, avalca1n empty, both spelled in lower case. Column names match case-insensitively on every surface (owner ruling 2026-09-28), so the lowercase spelling a SAS dataset may carry satisfies the Requirements.Variables.All templates and the rule executes with the same verdict as on the uppercase twin (CDISC-AD0437-invalid): CR437 — AVALCAyN is not populated where AVALCATy is (ADaMIG 1.3 Table 3.3.4.1, one-to-one mapping) -> violation."
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=01-701-1015
# Declared-tier scope: the class= declaration disagrees with the columns, so #define must
# carry it to RuleRunner (ScenarioDeclaredScopeProvider.install).
#define standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col avalcat1 type=Char
col avalca1n type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | VAL |
---
